Shanu Danu-Vavich Intro (Galen's character a wood elf druid)

Intro from Notes:
Shanu of the Ingrevassa Tribe was born under whispering pines and silvered boughs, in the deep woods of a peninsula of the Wealdath that juts like a claw into the Sea of Swords. The Wood Elves of this place live close to the roots of the world, and none more so than Shanu. A young druid walking the path of balance, he is well-regarded among his kin—not yet fully inducted into the Circle, but watched closely by its elders.
Like all in his season of growth, he has taken on the mantle of responsibility: patrolling the sacred boundaries of their land, tending to the health of grove and glade, and watching for the signs of monsters… or men.
Tonight, dusk is settling like a hush over the forest. The last light falls sideways through the trees in long, golden beams. The breeze smells of brine and pine needles. A small creeks gurgle along the shoreline. Water pure, cold, and fast, spilling down a rocky shelves in waterfalls before feeding into the narrows beach on the peninsula’s north shore.
A party of young warriors patrols the coastline, a day’s way from the homesteads and villages they reside in.

Two rowboats have landed on the sand, beached just above the tide line. Near the creek, a handful of goblins—five or six—squat and jostle with barrels and skins, filling them with fresh water. They bark and grumble in a harsh, high-pitched tongue.
Standing a short distance away is a single orc, arms crossed, watching them with a stern gaze. His leather coat bears strange insignias—nautical, foreign—and a rusted cutlass hangs from his belt. He does not help them. He guards them.
They haven't seen you.
The beach is exposed, but the treeline gives you cover. The tide murmurs. Somewhere offshore, hidden by the headland, a ship likely waits.
This is sacred land.
They are intruders.

