The opening for Galen's character Shanu took place when he and a band of warriors from his Tribe ambushed some pirate orcs and goblins that had come to shore for fresh water and other foraging. They were patrolling along the Northern shores of the dragon's neck when they came upon the trespassers.

They fought and defeated the sum of the over 2 dozen enemies, with only a pair of their brethren falling, though many sustained injuries.

They monitored the orcish slaver barge which then set sail west, hugging the coastline. Knowing that the ship would soon come upon a cluster of neighboring tribe's fishing villages, they ran swiftly ahead, cross-country, to warn their neighbors and to muster their defenses.
With their remaining members and archers from village well warned and prepared, they waited for the ship to approach close enough around a rocky cape, before ambushing the ship and boarding it with the villages fishing boats, covered by archers firing waves of arrows from the cliffs.
They managed to defeat every last greenskinned slaver, and released more than 20 captives from far-flung origins and nearby villages alike.

With a skeleton crew consisting of the foreign blooded captives, after resting for some time, Shanu decided to sail the orcish vessel west to the town of men called Velen.

Crewing an orcish ship proved very difficult, given it's crude and brutish construction, meant for and built by creatures who lack much wit, but make up for it doubly in the stamina and strength.

It would take them a tenday, but Shanu would eventually arrive in Velen, where the third session would begin!

